@gene("a8", "a step downhill on the walking field to GOAL, penalised for ending near enemy champions", parents=["a8"])
def move_value(o: Option) -> Num:
    g = step_gain(o.tile)
    if g <= 0:
        return 0
    risk = count(1 for u in enemies() if dist(u.pos, o.tile) <= 2)
    return max(10, 100 + 10 * g - 40 * risk)
```

This mutates `walk_field` (w5) so the walking field also routes around visible enemy champions. Units already block their own tiles, but the field currently walks right past them, so retreats and bank walks can end up adjacent to an enemy. I also keep the goal and my own tile open so the search can still start and finish. `here` is unchanged.

